WHISKEY COMPANY


Whiskey Company was an elite Marine Corps unit created to carry out highly dangerous operations. One of the unit's primary missions was to capture the war criminal Roland Kane, who was hiding on a remote terraformed planet. The unit included Joseph Turok, a former member of the elite Wolf Pack unit and a close acquaintance of Kane himself.

The unit was a well-armed combat team capable of operating in the harshest conditions. Whiskey Company was equipped with assault and pulse rifles, shotguns, machine guns, sniper weapons, grenade launchers, flamethrowers, explosives, and combat knives. The unit included command staff, medics, heavy infantry, engineers, and pilots, allowing them to conduct independent operations away from the main forces.

However, the operation against Kane went awry from the very beginning. While approaching the planet, Whiskey Company's ship was shot down by a Mendel-Gruman anti-aircraft system and crashed to the surface, breaking into several pieces. The survivors found themselves scattered among a jungle inhabited by genetically modified dinosaurs, giant insects, and other predators. Mendel-Gruman soldiers simultaneously began hunting them.

Despite the disaster, the remnants of Whiskey Company were able to regroup and establish a temporary camp. But escaping the planet proved nearly impossible: one after another, the soldiers perished from Mendel-Gruman fire, attacks by dinosaurs, and other creatures. Only a few of the original unit survived the carnage and escaped the planet. For Whiskey Company, the mission to capture Kane became a struggle for survival, where the enemy could be anyone-a soldier, a predator, or the planet itself.
